By applying the expectation over samples and using the result from \citet{horowitz1994mean}, we have
    \begin{align}\label{eq:thm:exp-wp}
        \mathbb{E} W_p(\mu,\hat\mu_n) \leq \frac{1}{\alpha} \mathbb{E} W_p(T_\#\mu, T_\#\hat\mu_n) \leq \frac{C_2 n^{-2/(d+4)}}{\alpha}
    \end{align}
    where $C_2$ depends only on $T_\#\mu$ and $d$.

    Combining \eqref{eq:thm-wp-discrete}, \eqref{eq:wp-tria}, and \eqref{eq:thm:exp-wp}, we get the desired result.
